From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Wed, 1 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] staging: fbtft: keep the panel content at registration

fbtft_register_framebuffer() flushes the newly allocated, zeroed
framebuffer to the panel. When the boot loader has already initialised
the controller and drawn a boot logo, that clears the screen to black.

Drop the initial full-display update. init_display(), set_var() and
set_gamma() still bring the controller up; they touch controller
registers, not display RAM, so the panel keeps its content until
userspace draws. Runtime updates through deferred I/O are unaffected.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/staging/fbtft/fbtft-core.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/fbtft/fbtft-core.c b/drivers/staging/fbtft/fbtft-core.c
index eac1d570f..dd0b4c9be 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/fbtft/fbtft-core.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/fbtft/fbtft-core.c
@@ -818,8 +818,12 @@ int fbtft_register_framebuffer(struct fb_info *fb_info)
 			goto reg_fail;
 	}
 
-	/* update the entire display */
-	par->fbtftops.update_display(par, 0, par->info->var.yres - 1);
+	/*
+	 * No initial full-display update: the framebuffer starts zeroed, and
+	 * flushing it would clear what the boot loader drew on the panel. The
+	 * panel keeps its content until userspace draws; runtime updates are
+	 * unaffected.
+	 */
 
 	if (par->fbtftops.set_gamma && par->gamma.curves) {
 		ret = par->fbtftops.set_gamma(par, par->gamma.curves);
-- 
